  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p><strong>Aura</strong> faint Warp; <strong>CL</strong> 3rd<br>\n<strong>Slot</strong> none; <strong>Price</strong> 200 gp; <strong>Weight</strong> 1/2&nbsp;lb.</p>\n<p><strong>Description</strong><br>\nThis small cloth bag easily fits in the hand, but opens into an extradimensional space that can store up to 1 cubic foot of material or 10 pounds. They can also be designed as pockets and sewn into normal or magical clothing.</p>\n<p><strong>Construction Requirements</strong><br>\nCraft Apparatus, Warp sphere (Extradimensional Storage (space)); <strong>Cost</strong> 100 gp</p>\n<p><a href=\"http://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/apparatuses#toc34\">Source: Spheres of Power Wiki</a></p>",
      "instructions": "<p>Reviewed profile: published apparatus with source-specific limits.</p><p>Empty hand-sized cloth bag or sewn-in pocket. Track both the one-cubic-foot and ten-pound storage limits; do not convert volume to an invented larger weight capacity. No contents are bundled. The source does not explicitly state a carried-weight exemption, so no automatic weight reduction is borrowed from a conventional Bag of Holding.</p>",
